  "nl_text": "The rschema_0175 database is designed to track donations and projects within an organization. The alumni table stores information about individual alumni, including their name, employer, job title, department, class, enrollment year, and ID number, with each record uniquely identified by a unique alumni ID. The employer field references the unit table, which contains information about different units within the organization, identified by a unique unit ID. The donation record table captures details of donations made by alumni, including the donating alumni's ID, donation time, amount, type, and usage, with each record uniquely identified by a unique donation ID. The project table stores information about individual projects, including the project ID, name, start and end times, and total donation amount. The benefit detail table links projects to the units they benefit, specifying the percentage of the donation allocated to each unit, with each record uniquely identified by a combination of the beneficiary unit and project ID. The donation project table serves as a bridge between the donation record and project tables, linking each donation to the corresponding project.",
  "gold_question": "The system shall record alumni personal information, including Alumni ID, Name, Employer, Job Title, Department, Class, Enrollment Year, and ID Number. The donation management module shall record detailed information for each donation, including Donation ID, Donating Alumni, Donation Time, Donation Amount, Donation Type (such as one-time donation or recurring donation), and Donation Usage (such as sponsoring individuals or funding projects). Additionally, the system shall record basic information for each donation project, including Project ID, Project Name, and Start and End Time. Each project involves multiple beneficiary units, recording the benefit percentage for each unit and the specific benefit amount obtained by that unit from the project. Through the management of this information, the system shall effectively track the allocation and usage of alumni donations.",
  "input_json": "/data/RSchema_ExpResults4/Experiment2/schema2text_llama31/0175.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0175\nCREATE TABLE `alumni` (\n  `alumni_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `employer_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `job_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `department` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `class` varchar(50) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `enrollment_year` int(4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`alumni_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `alumni_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`employer_id`) REFERENCES `unit` (`unit_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `unit` (\n  `unit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `unit_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`unit_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `donation_record` (\n  `donation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `alumni_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `donation_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `amount` decimal(10,2) NOT NULL,\n  `donation_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `usage` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`donation_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `donation_record_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`alumni_id`) REFERENCES `alumni` (`alumni_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `project` (\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  `total_donation_amount` decimal(10,2) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`project_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `benefit_detail` (\n  `unit_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `percentage` decimal(5,2) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`unit_id`, `project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `benefit_detail_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`unit_id`) REFERENCES `unit` (`unit_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `benefit_detail_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `donation_project` (\n  `donation_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `project_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`donation_id`, `project_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `donation_project_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`donation_id`) REFERENCES `donation_record` (`donation_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `donation_project_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`project_id`) REFERENCES `project` (`project_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
